{"id":"hdf-d7m","title":"Add ARF (Asset Reporting Format) support to XCCDF converter","description":"ARF (NIST IR 7694) is an XML wrapper format that packages one or more XCCDF TestResults along with asset metadata (IP, hostname, FQDN) and relationships. OpenSCAP and other SCAP scanners produce ARF as their primary output format.\n\nThe XCCDF converter should be extended to:\n1. Detect whether input is raw XCCDF or ARF-wrapped XCCDF (root element is arf:asset-report-collection vs xccdf:Benchmark/TestResult)\n2. If ARF: extract all arf:report elements containing xccdf:TestResult, extract asset metadata from arf:assets, and delegate each TestResult to existing XCCDF conversion logic\n3. Produce a multi-baseline HDF output when multiple TestResults exist (one baseline per report)\n4. Enrich HDF targets with ARF asset identification (IP addresses, MAC addresses, FQDN, hostname)\n5. Register 'arf' as a CLI alias for the xccdf converter (similar to inspec-to-hdf aliasing legacyhdf)\n\nKey ARF structure:\n- Root: arf:asset-report-collection\n- arf:report-requests — embeds or references the benchmark used\n- arf:assets — computing-device with IP/MAC/FQDN/hostname\n- arf:reports — contains one or more arf:report, each wrapping an xccdf:TestResult\n- core:relationships — links reports to assets via arfvocab:isAbout\n\nSchema: https://csrc.nist.gov/schema/asset-reporting-format/1.1/asset-reporting-format_1.1.0.xsd\nSpec: https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/IR/nistir7694.pdf\n\nThe new findXmlValues utility from hdf-utilities is well-suited for traversing ARF's nested structure to locate TestResult elements and asset metadata.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-23T02:46:59Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-23T02:46:59Z"}
