{"id":"hdf-libs-07n","title":"hdf-parsers: improve mutation test coverage (36 survived, 38 no-cov)","description":"Stryker mutation testing scored hdf-parsers at **50.00%** (36 survived, 38 no-coverage) when run on unit tests only. Integration tests were excluded because Stryker's sandbox doesn't include sibling-package fixture files. Stryker config is at `hdf-parsers/stryker.config.cjs`.\n\n## Root cause of low score\nMost survivors and all no-coverage mutations are in code paths only exercised by `integration.test.ts`, which reads fixture files from `hdf-converters/converters/hdf-to-xml/fixtures/`. Stryker cannot reach these files from its `.stryker-tmp` sandbox.\n\n## Cluster 1: Trailing-garbage detection (36 survived / uncovered)\n`parseResults`, `parseBaseline`, and `autoDetect` all have:\n```ts\nconst trimmedInput = jsonStr.trim();\n// ... parse ...\nif (serialized.length !== trimmedInput.length \u0026\u0026 !isWhitespaceEquivalent(serialized, trimmedInput)) {\n  return { success: false, error: 'Input contains trailing data...' }\n}\n```\nEvery operator and boolean in this condition survived because unit tests don't include inputs with trailing garbage.\n\n## Cluster 2: Schema validation failure path (3 survived)\n`if (!validationResult.valid)` and the error message body survive — unit tests don't pass structurally invalid JSON (valid JSON, wrong HDF structure).\n\n## Cluster 3: `autoDetect` type narrowing (4 survived)\n`typeof data === 'object' \u0026\u0026 data !== null` and `'name' in obj \u0026\u0026 'requirements' in obj` survive — unit tests don't call `autoDetect` with an object that lacks these keys.\n\n## Cluster 4: `isWhitespaceEquivalent` (38 no-coverage)\nEntire helper function never called by unit tests.\n\n## Fix options\n1. **Preferred**: Add unit tests that exercise the above paths directly — pass trailing-garbage JSON, invalid-schema JSON, and objects missing `name`/`requirements`. This avoids the sandbox issue entirely.\n2. **Alternative**: Configure Stryker to include `hdf-converters` fixture files in its sandbox via `symlinkNodeModules: false` and a custom file pattern — complex, may break other things.\n\n## Priority\nMedium — the integration tests do cover these paths, so production correctness is verified. This is a test infrastructure gap, not a correctness gap.","status":"closed","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-18T22:30:00Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:45Z","closed_at":"2026-02-18T23:28:15Z"}
