{"id":"hdf-libs-0n1","title":"Build HDF v1.0 to v2.0 converter","description":"Create converter from HDF v1.0 to v2.0 format to validate that the new schema can handle all v1.0 use cases. This shakes out schema viability before building other libraries.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","created_at":"2025-12-30T22:11:20.546116-05:00","updated_at":"2026-02-25T22:28:42.570354-05:00","closed_at":"2026-01-13T15:29:31Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-0n1","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-kze","type":"blocks","created_at":"2026-01-03T16:10:02.180277-05:00","created_by":"daemon"}],"comments":[{"id":1,"issue_id":"hdf-libs-0n1","author":"wdower","text":"APPROACH DECIDED: Building proper library skeletons to support v1→v2 converter.\n\nPlan:\n1. Build hdf-utilities skeleton (JSON utilities only, no XML/CSV yet)\n2. Build hdf-mappings skeleton (CCI/NIST data + basic lookup)\n3. Build v1→v2 converter in hdf-converters\n\nThis validates the pattern for all future converters and ensures proper architecture.\n\nBranch: Renamed hdf-schema → hdf-libs-development","created_at":"2026-01-03T21:09:41Z"},{"id":2,"issue_id":"hdf-libs-0n1","author":"wdower","text":"SESSION STATUS (pre-compaction):\n\nCOMPLETED:\n- hdf-utilities skeleton: JSON parsing utilities, 100% test coverage, peer-reviewed (A- grade)\n- All major peer review issues fixed: vitest.config.ts, ESLint, type-check script, 100% coverage\n- hdf-schema coverage raised from 70% to 95% (now 100% actual coverage, 406 tests passing)\n- Branch: hdf-libs-development (renamed from hdf-schema)\n- All commits signed and pushed\n\nNEXT STEPS:\n1. Build hdf-mappings skeleton (hdf-libs-2c1) - CCI/NIST data + lookup functions\n2. Then build v1→v2 structural transformation (hdf-libs-kze) - depends on utilities + mappings\n3. Finally complete full converter with CLI\n\nKEY DECISIONS:\n- 95% coverage threshold standard for all runtime libraries\n- Build scripts (like hdf-schema) use c8 ignore comments for CLI entry points\n-