{"id":"hdf-libs-17i","title":"hdf-mappings (TS): improve mutation test coverage (67 survived)","description":"Stryker mutation testing scored hdf-mappings at **72.48%** (67 survived, 187 killed). Stryker config is at `hdf-mappings/stryker.config.cjs`.\n\n## Survived mutation clusters (affect all or most mapping files)\n\n### 1. Lazy-initialization null checks (8 files × 2 mutations = ~16 survived)\nEvery mapping module has `if (mappings === null) { mappings = JSON.parse(readFileSync(...)) }`. Mutating to `if (true)` survives because tests always hit a warm cache — the cold-init path is never independently tested.\n\n**Fix**: Add a test helper that resets the module-level cache variable to `null` between test runs, then assert the function still returns correct data after the reset.\n\n### 2. `'utf-8'` encoding argument (8 files × 1 mutation = ~8 survived)\n`readFileSync(path, 'utf-8')` — changing encoding to `\"\"` survives because the test doesn't verify encoding was honored. With `\"\"`, Node returns a Buffer; JSON.parse on a Buffer still works in most cases.\n\n**Fix**: This is somewhat inherent to how Node handles encoding — consider accepting this survivor as a known false positive, or test with a file containing non-ASCII characters to distinguish Buffer vs string parsing.\n\n### 3. Type guards `||` → `\u0026\u0026` (cci, nist, owasp — ~12 mutations)\nPattern: `if (!id || typeof id !== 'string')` — mutating `||` to `\u0026\u0026` survives because tests don't pass falsy non-string inputs (e.g., `null`, `0`, `false`). The `!id` check already handles those, so the `\u0026\u0026` mutation still rejects them.\n\n**Fix**: Add tests that pass `null`, `undefined`, `0`, `false`, and `123` (number) to each lookup function and assert they return the correct empty/null/false result.\n\n### 4. nikto `typeof id === 'number'` ternary (4 survived)\n`src/nikto/index.ts:30` — the `typeof niktoId === 'number' ? String(niktoId) : niktoId` coercion is not tested with a numeric argument. Tests only pass strings.\n\n**Fix**: Add a test that passes a numeric Nikto ID and verifies it's correctly coerced to a string for lookup.\n\n### 5. nessus exact/wildcard match logic (several survived)\n`src/nessus/index.ts` — the exact-match find predicate and wildcard fallback are weakly covered. The wildcard path (`pluginID === '*'`) is not covered at all (4 no-coverage mutations).\n\n**Fix**: Add test cases for: (a) an exact plugin family + ID match, (b) a wildcard match (pluginID === '*'), (c) no match (returns undefined).\n\n### 6. nist regex anchor (1 survived)\n`src/nist/index.ts:105` — `/^([A-Z]{2})-/` anchor removal survives — the `^` start anchor isn't tested with a string that has a prefix before the NIST family code.\n\n**Fix**: Test `getNISTFamily('prefix-AC-2')` and verify it returns the correct result (or no match if the regex requires start-of-string).","status":"closed","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-18T22:30:00Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:46Z","closed_at":"2026-02-18T23:28:15Z"}
