{"id":"hdf-libs-40e","title":"Make Requirement_Result.status required field","description":"The `Requirement_Result.status` field is currently optional/nullable but should be required. Every test execution produces a status (passed/failed/error/notApplicable/notReviewed).\n\n## Rationale\n- Every test result has a status outcome\n- Status is fundamental to understanding test results\n- Making it optional creates ambiguity\n- All converters already provide status\n\n## Changes Required\n\n### Schema Changes (TDD Approach)\n\n1. **Update tests first**\n   - Update test fixtures to always include status\n   - Add tests that reject results without status\n   - Verify all existing tests pass\n\n2. **Update schema**\n   - result.schema.json: Change status from `anyOf: [Result_Status, null]` to just `$ref: Result_Status`\n   - Add `status` to required fields in Requirement_Result\n   - Regenerate types\n\n3. **Update helpers**\n   - Ensure createResult helper always includes status\n   - Add validation that status is provided\n\n4. **Update converters**\n   - Verify all converters provide status\n   - sarif-to-hdf: Always set status based on result\n   - nessus-to-hdf: Always set status based on compliance result\n   - Add default status handling for edge cases\n\n### Files to Update\n- `hdf-schema/src/schemas/primitives/result.schema.json`\n- `hdf-schema/src/helpers.js`\n- `hdf-schema/src/helpers.d.ts`\n- `hdf-schema/test/hdf-results.test.ts`\n- All converter files\n- All converter test files\n\n### Validation\n- All existing converters already provide status\n- Check that no converter has code paths that omit status\n- Verify test coverage for status handling\n\n## Breaking Change\nThis is a breaking change but should have minimal impact as all current converters already provide status.\n\n## Priority\nMedium - Improves schema strictness and clarity","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-01T20:59:04Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:47Z","closed_at":"2026-02-04T20:37:04Z","close_reason":"Closed"}
{"id":"hdf-libs-41z","title":"Add inspec-to-hdf converter","description":"InSpec JSON output needs a dedicated converter for HDF v2. In v1, HDF was structurally derived from InSpec output format, so no converter was needed. In v2, a converter is required.\n\nInSpec JSON output format: { platform: {...}, profiles: [ { name, version, title, controls: [ { id, title, desc, impact, refs, tags, results: [...] } ] } ] }\n\nThis format is the same as the legacyhdf-to-hdf converter input. The inspec-to-hdf converter should:\n- Be a thin, well-named wrapper that clearly targets current InSpec output (v4/v5+)\n- Set dataSource.name = 'Chef InSpec' and dataSource.version from the InSpec version field in output\n- Handle multi-profile InSpec runs (one baseline per profile, or merged - TBD)\n- Handle wrapper profiles (InSpec profiles that depend on other profiles)\n- May share parsing logic with legacyhdf-to-hdf or may replace it once legacy migration is complete\n\nDesign question: should this share code with legacyhdf-to-hdf or be independent? The legacyhdf converter handles HDF v1 data that was already processed by Heimdall, which may differ slightly from raw InSpec output.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-20T16:57:36Z","created_by":"Will","updated_at":"2026-02-22T21:20:45Z","closed_at":"2026-02-22T21:20:45Z","close_reason":"Resolved via alias: InSpec exec-json is identical to HDF v1.0, so legacyhdf-to-hdf handles it. Added CLI alias (hdf convert inspec to hdf) in b1a1d8d and ubi9 STIG fixture in 686c001."}
{"id":"hdf-libs-4pt","title":"Verify all converter input fixtures against source format schemas","description":"Audit every converter's fixtures/input/ directory to ensure input files are real tool output or validate against the source format's schema/specification. Fabricated fixtures must be replaced with real tool output. Converters to check: gosec, nessus, sarif, sonarqube, aws-config, anchore-grype, legacyhdf, hdf-to-csv, hdf-to-xml, junit. For formats with formal schemas (SARIF, JUnit XML, CycloneDX, XCCDF), validate fixtures against the schema. For tool-specific formats (gosec JSON, Nessus XML), verify fixtures were sourced from real tool runs.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-21T15:37:40Z","created_by":"Will","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:48Z"}
{"id":"hdf-libs-5so","title":"Evaluate CSV injection risk for security tool converters","description":"Assess whether CSV formula injection (=, +, -, @, |, %) is a real threat for security tool output. Security tools may include user-controlled data (URLs, finding descriptions, plugin output). Decide: (1) Add sanitization to buildCsv/buildCsvArray to prefix dangerous chars with ', (2) Document risk and leave to converters, or (3) Accept risk as minimal for this use case. Research: check heimdall2 converters that output CSV.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-01-28T13:11:05Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:49Z","closed_at":"2026-01-28T13:21:07Z","close_reason":"Implemented CSV formula injection protection with opt-in sanitization. Added sanitizeCsvValue/Array/Object functions and 'sanitize' parameter to buildCsv/buildCsvArray. Protects against =+-@|% formula triggers. 19 new tests, all 163 tests passing. Backward compatible (default unchanged)."}
{"id":"hdf-libs-66d","title":"Implement SonarQube live fetch mode","description":"Add live API fetch mode to the SonarQube converter so users can run a single command instead of manually capturing the /api/issues/search response.\n\n## What\nhdf convert sonarqube to hdf --live --url https://sq.example.com --token TOKEN --project my-proj output.json\n\nThe fetcher lives in hdf-cli/internal/fetchers/sonarqube.go. It calls the SonarQube REST API (no extra Go deps — standard net/http), paginates /api/issues/search, and marshals the combined response into the same IssuesResponse format the file-based converter already reads. File-based mode continues to work unchanged.\n\n## API mocking\nTests must not require a live SonarQube server. Use httptest.Server serving canned JSON responses pointed at via --url flag. Coordinate with hdf-libs-6b0.21.2 (Improve SonarQube testing without live server).\n\n## Credentials / flags\n--url (required), --token (required), --project (required), --branch (optional), --org (optional), --insecure (skip TLS verify)","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-19T13:04:35Z","created_by":"Will","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:49Z","closed_at":"2026-02-20T15:21:29Z","close_reason":"Implemented in hdf-cli/internal/fetchers/sonarqube.go + fetch_sonarqube.go. Token via SONARQUBE_TOKEN env var (not --token flag). Pagination via ps=500, capped at 10k pages. httptest-based tests, no live server required.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-66d","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
