{"id":"hdf-libs-6b0.12","title":"Implement msft-secure-score converter","description":"Port Microsoft Secure Score converter from heimdall2. Convert tool output to HDF v2.0 format.\n\n## Completion requires both:\n1. File-based converter: accepts a combined JSON export with secureScore and secureScoreControlProfiles (matching the SAF CLI msft_secure2hdf --combined-input format)\n2. Live fetch mode: hdf convert msft-secure-score to hdf --live --tenant TENANT --app-id ID --app-secret SECRET output.json\n   - Fetcher in hdf-cli/internal/fetchers/msft_secure.go\n   - OAuth2 client credentials flow (tenant + app ID + secret -\u003e access token)\n   - Calls Microsoft Graph API: /security/secureScores and /security/secureScoreControlProfiles with pagination\n   - Uses golang.org/x/oauth2 for token exchange (avoid full Azure SDK)\n   - Marshals to the same static format the file-based converter reads\n\n## API mocking\nTests must not require live Azure credentials. Mock the OAuth2 token endpoint and Graph API endpoints via httptest.Server. Document the mock approach before implementing.\n\n## Note\nThis is the highest-effort live fetch of the set due to the OAuth2 flow. Consider implementing after simpler API converters to establish patterns.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-01-27T13:11:28Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-19T13:04:56Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.12","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
