{"id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.1","title":"Address SonarQube 10,000 record limit","description":"Filter-based partitioning for projects with true \u003e10,000 issues is not yet implemented.\n\nWhat was done: fetcher caps pagination at maxPages=10,000 (ps=500 per page = up to 5M issues). For most real projects this is sufficient.\n\nWhat remains: if a project hits the Elasticsearch 10k result limit on a single unfiltered query, the API will return at most 10,000 issues regardless of page count. To handle those projects, we need to split queries by severity/type/language/date range and merge results. This is the original scope of this issue.\n\nReference: https://community.sonarsource.com/t/how-to-retrieve-more-than-10-000-results-using-api-issues-search/153628","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-08T14:00:52Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-20T15:21:44Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.1","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
{"id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.2","title":"Improve SonarQube testing without live server","description":"Create static SonarQube API response fixtures (JSON files) instead of requiring a mock server. Mock API endpoints directly using MSW or similar for TypeScript/Go. Capture real SonarQube responses for different scenarios (branch, PR, main project).\n\nCurrent heimdall2 approach requires running 'yarn run cypress-test mock-json' to start a mock HTTP server on port 3001, which is cumbersome for testing.\n\nGoal: Enable converter testing with static fixtures, no server required.","notes":"Research completed 2026-02-10. See TESTING-RESEARCH.md in sonarqube-to-hdf directory.\n\nKey findings:\n- Our approach is already superior to Heimdall2 (static fixtures vs mock server)\n- DefectDojo provides gold standard with 17+ test fixtures covering edge cases\n- Need to expand fixtures: empty results, large datasets, hotspots, multiple projects\n- Should follow DefectDojo's pattern: real API captures, comprehensive edge cases\n- No mock server needed - static JSON is better (faster, reliable, version controlled)\n\nNext steps: Create expanded fixture set following recommendations in research doc.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-08T14:01:03Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-20T15:21:33Z","closed_at":"2026-02-20T15:21:33Z","close_reason":"All fetcher and converter tests use httptest.NewServer with canned JSON responses. contextCapturingSonarqubeTransport RoundTripper added to verify timeout behavior. No live SonarQube server required for any test.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.2","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
{"id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.3","title":"Support SonarQube Web API v2","description":"Add support for SonarQube Web API v2 endpoints (introduced in SonarQube Server 10.4+). Complete migration targeted for version 11.X LTS. Enhanced API access for SCA results and SBOMs.\n\nThe converter should detect and use v2 endpoints when available while maintaining backward compatibility with v1 API.\n\nHeimdall2 PR #6952 updated the converter in August 2025 with bearer token auth and version support for 8, 9, 10, and 2025.\n\nRelated:\n- https://www.sonarsource.com/blog/new-web-api-v2/\n- https://github.com/mitre/heimdall2/pull/6952","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-08T14:01:13Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-08T14:01:13Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.3","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
{"id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.4","title":"Handle multiple SonarQube versions","description":"Support SonarQube versions 8, 9, 10, and 25+ with version-specific type definitions and authentication methods:\n- Versions 8-10: Basic auth (token as username)\n- Version 25+: Bearer token authentication\n- Consider auto-detection of SonarQube version from API responses\n\nHeimdall2 implementation (PR #6952) already has version-specific types: Issue_8, Issue_9, Issue_10, and Rule_8, Rule_9, Rule_10, Rule_25.\n\nPort this version handling logic to hdf-libs implementation.\n\nReference: https://github.com/mitre/heimdall2/pull/6952","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-08T14:01:22Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-08T14:01:22Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.4","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
{"id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.5","title":"Create comprehensive SonarQube test fixtures","description":"Capture actual /api/issues/search, /api/sources/raw, and /api/rules/show responses from real SonarQube instances for testing.\n\nInclude edge cases:\n- Empty results (no issues found)\n- Large projects (approaching 10,000 limit)\n- Different issue types (bugs, vulnerabilities, code smells)\n- Branch analysis samples\n- Pull request scanning samples\n- Various severity levels\n\nCreate minimal, medium, and comprehensive test cases.\n\nCurrent heimdall2 test fixtures only contain HDF outputs, not SonarQube API inputs. We need the input side for proper testing.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-08T14:01:36Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-08T14:01:36Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.5","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
{"id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.6","title":"Continue SonarQube API format research","description":"Ongoing research into SonarQube API formats, version differences, and real-world response shapes.\n\nResearch already completed (2026-02-10) in hdf-converters/converters/sonarqube-to-hdf/TESTING-RESEARCH.md:\n- Confirmed static fixtures are superior to mock server approach\n- Identified DefectDojo as reference implementation\n- Mapped gaps in fixture coverage\n\nRemaining questions to investigate:\n- What changed between SonarQube v8/v9/v10/2025 API response formats?\n- Do security hotspots use a different API endpoint (api/hotspots/search)?\n- What does the SonarCloud API response look like vs on-prem?\n- Are there open datasets of real SonarQube API responses available?\n- How do SonarQube rules map to CWE/OWASP/NIST in practice across language analyzers?\n- What edge cases exist in real-world large projects (10k+ issues)?\n\nGoal: Inform fixture expansion for hdf-libs-6b0.21.5.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-17T23:46:55Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-20T15:21:38Z","closed_at":"2026-02-20T15:21:38Z","close_reason":"Key findings incorporated: (1) SonarQube timestamps use +0000 not +00:00 — fixed with custom format 2006-01-02T15:04:05-0700. (2) Impact mapping corrected (CRITICAL 0.9→0.7, INFO 0.3→0.0). (3) CWE→NIST lookup implemented via new hdf-mappings/go/cwe package. Remaining open questions (hotspots API, v8/v9/v10 diffs, SonarCloud) deferred to converter-level tasks.","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21.6","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.21","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
{"id":"hdf-libs-6b0.22","title":"Implement splunk converter","description":"Port Splunk converter from heimdall2. Convert HDF data stored in Splunk back to HDF format.\n\n## Completion requires both:\n1. File-based converter: accepts a JSON export of Splunk search results containing HDF data\n2. Live fetch mode: hdf convert splunk to hdf --live --host HOST --port 8089 --token TOKEN --file GUID output.json\n   - Fetcher in hdf-cli/internal/fetchers/splunk.go\n   - Splunk REST API: authenticate (username/password or bearer token), run search job, retrieve results\n   - Supports listing available HDF executions (omit --file to list) as well as fetching a specific one\n   - Marshals to the same static format the file-based converter reads\n\n## API mocking\nTests must not require a live Splunk instance. Mock via httptest.Server. Document the mock approach before implementing.\n\n## Credentials / flags\n--host (required), --port (default 8089), --scheme (http/https, default https), --token OR --username + --password (one required), --file (GUID to fetch; omit to list available), --insecure","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-01-27T13:11:29Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-19T13:05:02Z","dependencies":[{"issue_id":"hdf-libs-6b0.22","depends_on_id":"hdf-libs-6b0","type":"parent-child","created_at":"2026-02-22T19:18:39Z","created_by":"bootstrap","metadata":"{}"}]}
