{"id":"hdf-libs-73r","title":"HDF schema: separate data-source from tool-creator in Generator","description":"The current Generator field conflates two distinct concepts: (1) the source tool that produced the original scan data (e.g. Nessus, gosec, SonarQube) and (2) the software that actually created the HDF file (e.g. hdf-converters, hdf-cli). Both need to be representable independently so consumers can determine provenance without inspecting converter internals.\n\nProposed change: split Generator into two fields or sub-fields:\n- source (or dataSource): name/version of the original scanning tool\n- converter (or creator): name/version of the HDF-producing tool\n\nThis is a schema-level change (hdf-schema) with downstream impact on:\n- hdf-schema: TypeScript type definitions and JSON schema\n- hdf-schema Go package: struct definitions\n- hdf-validators: update validation rules for new/renamed fields\n- hdf-converters (all converters, both Go and TypeScript): update Generator construction\n- hdf-cli: update CLI version injection\n- hdf-parsers: update any field references\n- Possibly hdf-to-csv, hdf-to-xml output-side converters\n\nDesign questions to resolve before implementation:\n- New top-level fields vs nested under existing Generator?\n- Backwards compatibility: is the old Generator field deprecated or removed?\n- Field names: source/converter, dataSource/creator, or something else?\n- Version field: does each sub-field carry its own version, or shared?\n- How should converters that have no meaningful 'source version' (e.g. static file import) populate the source field?","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-20T16:47:03Z","created_by":"Will","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:50Z","closed_at":"2026-02-20T21:28:44Z","close_reason":"Implemented as dataSource field on HdfResults (schema + all converters) in commits 7c2f694 and 1a4a878."}
