{"id":"hdf-libs-86e","title":"Review converter output for unnecessary null fields","description":"SYSTEMATIC REFACTOR: Nullable vs Optional Fields in HDF Schema\n\n## Problem Statement\nThe HDF schema currently uses nullable patterns (\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]) for 123 fields across all schemas. This was originally intended to make fields optional, but in JSON Schema, nullable means \"required to be present, but can have null value.\" This causes:\n- Verbose output with explicit null values for unused fields\n- Confusion about semantic intent\n- Incompatibility with Go omitempty tags\n- Wasted bytes in serialized JSON\n\n## Current State\nTotal nullable fields: 123\n- \"type\": [\"type\", \"null\"]\" pattern: 96 fields\n- \"anyOf\": [{$ref or type}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]\" pattern: 27 fields\n\nDistribution:\n- common.schema.json: ~40 fields\n- target.schema.json: ~50 fields\n- result.schema.json: ~5 fields (runTime, resource, resourceId, message, exception, backtrace, status)\n- hdf-results.schema.json: ~5 fields (depends, parentBaseline, description, inspecVersion, statusMessage)\n- hdf-baseline.schema.json: ~2 fields (depends, remediation)\n- extensions.schema.json: ~6 fields\n- statistics.schema.json: ~7 fields\n- platform.schema.json: ~1 field\n\n## Observed Issues\nFrom compliance.nessus conversion:\n1. depends: null (1 occurrence at baseline level)\n2. backtrace: null (5 occurrences at result level)\n\nThese should be omitted entirely when not provided.\n\n## Root Cause\nSchema design misunderstanding: nullable ≠ optional in JSON Schema.\n\nFor optional fields that can be omitted:\n- DON'T: \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"] with field not in required array\n- DO: \"type\": \"string\" with field not in required array\n\nThe nullable pattern makes serializers include \"field\": null in output.\n\n## Systematic Audit Plan\n\n### Phase 1: Categorize All 123 Nullable Fields\nFor each field, determine:\n1. Truly nullable (semantic difference between absent and null)\n   - Example: status field where null = \"not determined\" vs absent = \"not applicable\"\n2. Should be optional (no semantic difference, just omit when not present)\n   - Metadata: title, description, version\n   - Result details: backtrace, resource, resourceId, exception, message\n   - Baseline metadata: depends, parentBaseline, statusMessage\n3. Required with defaults (converters should always populate)\n\n### Phase 2: Update Schemas (TDD Approach)\nFor each field categorized as \"should be optional\":\n1. Update tests first to expect omission (not null)\n2. Change schema:\n   - \"type\": [\"primitive\", \"null\"] → \"type\": \"primitive\"\n   - \"anyOf\": [{...}, {\"type\": \"null\"}] → {...}\n3. Regenerate types from schema\n4. Update helpers/converters to conditionally include fields\n5. Verify tests pass\n\n### Phase 3: Update Converters\nFor each converter (sarif-to-hdf, nessus-to-hdf, etc.):\n- TypeScript: Conditional object construction (only add fields when present)\n- Go: Verify omitempty tags work correctly after regeneration\n- Update tests to verify omission behavior\n\n### Phase 4: Documentation\n- Document nullable vs optional distinction in schema README\n- Add examples of when to use each pattern\n- Update converter development guide\n\n## Files to Audit\n- hdf-schema/src/schemas/primitives/common.schema.json\n- hdf-schema/src/schemas/primitives/target.schema.json\n- hdf-schema/src/schemas/primitives/result.schema.json\n- hdf-schema/src/schemas/primitives/extensions.schema.json\n- hdf-schema/src/schemas/primitives/statistics.schema.json\n- hdf-schema/src/schemas/primitives/platform.schema.json\n- hdf-schema/src/schemas/hdf-results.schema.json\n- hdf-schema/src/schemas/hdf-baseline.schema.json\n\n## Expected Outcome\n- Cleaner JSON output with no unnecessary null fields\n- Clear semantic distinction between truly nullable and optional fields\n- Better Go omitempty compatibility\n- Smaller serialized JSON files\n- Clearer schema intent for developers\n\n## Priority\nMedium - Not critical for functionality, but impacts:\n- Data quality and readability\n- Schema clarity and maintainability\n- Output file size\n- Developer experience\n\n## Notes\n- Start with depends and backtrace as proof-of-concept\n- Most fields will likely become truly optional\n- Few (if any) fields have true semantic need for null vs absent distinction\n","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-01T20:05:33Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:50Z","closed_at":"2026-02-06T11:00:33Z","close_reason":"Closed"}
