{"id":"hdf-libs-c0r","title":"Add omitempty tags to Go type generation for discriminated unions","description":"Fix Go JSON output to match schema discriminated union intent by adding omitempty tags to optional fields.\n\nProblem:\n- Target uses oneOf discriminated union (Host, Container, Cloud, etc.)\n- quicktype generates single Go struct with all union fields\n- Without omitempty, Go marshals all nil fields as null\n- Result: Host target outputs 37 fields (35 nulls) instead of 7 relevant fields\n\nSolution:\n- Update hdf-schema type generation to add omitempty tags to optional fields\n- Ensures only populated fields appear in JSON output\n- Matches schema semantic intent of discriminated unions\n\nApproach (TDD):\n1. Write test that asserts omitempty tags exist on generated types\n2. Write test that validates marshaled JSON only contains non-null fields\n3. Update quicktype generation or post-processing to add omitempty\n4. Verify all converters produce cleaner output\n\nAffects:\n- hdf-schema/src/generators/go.ts (type generation)\n- All converters using Target, EvaluatedBaseline, etc.\n- Should be backward compatible (omitting nulls does not break consumers)","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"bug","created_at":"2026-01-29T16:33:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T14:37:36Z","closed_at":"2026-01-29T14:37:36Z","labels":["go","schema","type-generation"]}
