{"id":"hdf-libs-j7l","title":"Converters (Go): improve test coverage for sonarqube, anchore-grype, hdf-to-csv","description":"Gremlins mutation testing identified uncovered mutation clusters in three Go converters. All other converters scored 100% mutant coverage.\n\n## sonarqube-to-hdf (3 uncovered, 88.5% coverage)\n- `converter.go:289` — `if !hasRule || rule == nil` condition (extractDescription entry guard)\n- `converter.go:329` — inside the tag-splitting loop, the `allTagsMap[category]` nil check\n- `converter.go:424` — component path fallback (`component.Path` vs `component.LongName`)\n\n**Fix**: Add a test case where a SonarQube issue has no associated rule (rule=nil), and one where a component has only a `longName` but no `path`.\n\n## anchore-grype-to-hdf (2 uncovered, 94.9% coverage)\n- `converter.go:146` — `for _, related := range relatedVulns { if related.ID == vuln.ID \u0026\u0026 related.Description != \"\" }` — the related-vulnerability description fallback\n\n**Fix**: Add a fixture/test case where the primary vulnerability has no description but a related vulnerability with the same ID does have one.\n\n## hdf-to-csv (6 uncovered, 78.6% coverage)\n- `converter.go:171` — array-valued severity tag: `if arr, ok := sev.([]interface{}); ok \u0026\u0026 len(arr) \u003e 0`\n- `converter.go:181` — `if impact \u003e= 0.7` boundary (impact-to-severity derivation)\n- `converter.go:184` — `if impact \u003e= 0.4` boundary\n\n**Fix**: Add test controls with: (a) array-valued severity tags, (b) impact exactly at 0.7, (c) impact exactly at 0.4, (d) impact below 0.4 but above 0.\n\n## Re-running\nGremlins is installed at `~/go/bin/gremlins`. Run with `--timeout-coefficient 20` in each converter's `go/` directory.\n\n## Resolution\nAdded `TestExtractDescription` (nil rule, hasRule=false, HTMLDesc-only, Name fallback), `TestComponentPathResolution` (Path/LongName/missing component), `TestExtractTags_KeyValueParsing` (allTagsMap nil-check) to sonarqube converter_test.go. Added `TestGetVulnDescription_RelatedFallback` (primary empty → related fallback, unrelated ID, empty related desc) to anchore-grype converter_test.go. Added `TestGetSeverity_ArrayPath` ([]interface{} severity, impact boundaries 0.7/0.4/0.39) to hdf-to-csv converter_test.go. All tests pass.","status":"closed","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-18T22:30:00Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:54Z","closed_at":"2026-02-18T23:28:15Z"}
