{"id":"hdf-libs-n09","title":"hdf-validators: update import assertions to 'with' syntax","description":"The `typescript/index.ts` file uses deprecated `assert { type: 'json' }` import attribute syntax (lines 5–12) for JSON schema imports. This should be updated to the modern `with { type: 'json' }` syntax.\n\n## Why\n- `assert` is deprecated in the ECMAScript spec; `with` is the current standard\n- Stryker 9.x's Babel-based instrumenter cannot parse `assert { type: 'json' }` — this blocks mutation testing on hdf-validators entirely\n- Updating unblocks Stryker and aligns with the current standard\n\n## Changes Required\n- `hdf-validators/typescript/index.ts`: change all `assert { type: 'json' }` → `with { type: 'json' }` on JSON schema imports\n- Verify `pnpm test` still passes after the change\n- Re-run `npx stryker run` with `hdf-validators/stryker.config.cjs` to confirm Stryker can now instrument the file\n\n## Related\n- Stryker config already exists at `hdf-validators/stryker.config.cjs`\n\n## Resolution\nAll 9 `assert { type: 'json' }` import attributes changed to `with { type: 'json' }` in `hdf-validators/typescript/index.ts`. Pure syntax change; no logic affected.","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-18T22:30:00Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:55Z","closed_at":"2026-02-18T23:28:15Z"}
