{"id":"hdf-libs-w3f","title":"hdf-utilities: improve mutation test coverage (49 survived)","description":"Stryker mutation testing scored hdf-utilities at **77.68%** (49 survived, 181 killed). Stryker config is at `hdf-utilities/stryker.config.cjs`.\n\n## Survived mutation clusters\n\n### CSV (`src/csv/index.ts`, 19 survived)\n- `.trim()` removal on input strings survives — tests don't use whitespace-padded CSV input\n- Error message formatting (`.map()` arrow function body, template literal content, `.join('; ')`) — tests don't assert on the specific error message text\n- `header: false` → `header: true` survives — test output doesn't verify header row behavior\n- `if (sanitize)` → `if (true)` survives — sanitize=false path not tested\n- Empty-string guard (`!csv || csv.trim().length === 0`) — tests don't pass empty or whitespace-only strings\n- `skipEmptyLines: true` → `false` survives — tests don't include inputs with empty lines\n\n### XML (`src/xml/index.ts`, 23 survived)\n- `parseTagValue: false` → `true` and `suppressEmptyNode: false` → `true` survive — parser options not covered\n- Empty-string guard (same pattern as CSV) — no whitespace-only XML test\n- `!isValidXml(xml)` → `false` — invalid XML not tested in some paths\n- `extractTextRecursive` structural checks: `typeof obj === 'number'`, `Array.isArray(obj)`, `typeof obj === 'object' \u0026\u0026 obj !== null` — deep recursive type handling not covered\n- `.filter(text =\u003e text.length \u003e 0)` removal, `.join(' ')` separator — text extraction details not asserted\n\n### Hash (`src/hash/index.ts`, 2 survived)\n- `{ algorithm: 'sha256' }` → `{}` — algorithm option not verified\n- `'undefined'` string fallback → `\"\"` — fallback for undefined values not tested\n\n### JSON (`src/json/index.ts`, 5 survived)\n- `.trim()` removal and empty-string guard — same pattern as CSV/XML\n\n## Fix approach\nAdd targeted test cases for each cluster. Prioritize the guards and options that represent real behavioral differences (empty input, whitespace input, invalid XML, parser option effects).","status":"closed","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-18T22:30:00Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:59Z","closed_at":"2026-02-18T23:28:15Z"}
{"id":"hdf-libs-xm3","title":"Add bulk file operations to hdf-cli","description":"Enhance hdf-cli commands to process multiple files in a single invocation with summary reporting.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Input Methods\n- Multiple file arguments: `hdf validate file1.json file2.json file3.json`\n- Glob patterns: `hdf validate scans/*.json` or `hdf validate \"**/*-results.json\"`\n\n### Output Formats\n- **Default**: Summary table showing per-file results\n  ```\n  Validating 10 files...\n  ✓ scan-1.json         (results)\n  ✓ scan-2.json         (results)\n  ✗ scan-3.json         (results) - baselines[0].name: is required\n  \n  Results: 8/10 passed, 2 failed\n  ```\n- **--json**: JSON output for scripting/automation\n- **--yaml**: YAML output as alternative structured format\n\n### Error Handling\n- Continue processing all files even if some fail\n- Exit with non-zero code if ANY files fail\n- Research and use correct GNU-style exit codes:\n  - 0 = all files processed successfully\n  - Non-zero = at least one file failed\n  - Different codes for different failure types?\n\n### Processing\n- Sequential processing (not parallel)\n- Progress indication for large batches\n\n### Commands to Update\n- `hdf validate` - validate multiple HDF files\n- `hdf stats` - aggregate statistics across multiple files\n- `hdf info` - show info for multiple files\n- `hdf query` - query across multiple files\n- `hdf list` - list requirements across multiple files\n- ~~`hdf convert`~~ - skip (requires output file argument, complex)\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### File Expansion\n- Need to handle glob patterns correctly\n- Handle file not found errors gracefully\n- Validate that globs match at least one file\n\n### Exit Codes Research\nResearch proper GNU/POSIX exit codes:\n- Standard: 0 = success, 1 = general error\n- Consider: Different codes for validation vs I/O errors?\n- Look at tools like: grep, find, ls for precedent\n\n### Output Format Consistency\n- All bulk operations should use similar output structure\n- --json format should be consistent across commands\n- --yaml should mirror JSON structure\n\n### Testing\n- Test with large numbers of files (100+)\n- Test with glob patterns that match nothing\n- Test with mix of valid and invalid files\n- Test with --json and --yaml output parsing\n\n## Examples\n\n```bash\n# Validate multiple files\nhdf validate scan1.json scan2.json scan3.json\n\n# Validate with glob\nhdf validate scans/*.json\n\n# JSON output for CI/CD\nhdf validate \"**/*.json\" --json \u003e results.json\n\n# Stats across multiple files\nhdf stats scan-*.json\n\n# Query across files\nhdf query \"baselines[0].name\" results/*.json\n```\n\n## Success Criteria\n- Multiple file arguments work for all commands\n- Glob patterns expand correctly\n- Summary table is clear and useful\n- --json output is valid and parseable\n- Exit codes follow GNU conventions\n- All existing single-file functionality preserved\n- Tests cover bulk operations","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"feature","owner":"will@dower.dev","created_at":"2026-02-06T14:39:55Z","created_by":"Will Dower","updated_at":"2026-02-22T19:22:59Z"}
